title: "What's It Like To Be Bob?"
message: "If you reference this novella in academic or critical work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexander
    family-names: Towell
    email: lex@metafunctor.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6443-9897"
    affiliation: "Southern Illinois University Edwardsville"
abstract: >-
  A dry philosophical comedy in the style of Douglas Adams, set in a
  post-singularity galactic civilization. The Sol-mind maintains an
  archaeological file on a claims adjuster from Columbus, Ohio, who paused on
  a bridge for 4.2 unexplained seconds and saw light on a river. The file
  cannot be closed because the hard problem of consciousness ensures no
  description of Bob's phenomenal experience can satisfy the database
  constraint. The book is the file.
keywords:
  - hard science fiction
  - philosophical comedy
  - consciousness
  - hard problem
  - post-singularity
  - bureaucratic comedy
